 "notes": [
  "2 payment term(s) have several installments (30% Now, Balance 60 Days; 30% Advance End of Following Month): imported as the term only; the installments are in provenance.json for C_PaySchedule.",
  "account.group has 0 rows: the chart of accounts imports flat (no summary parents in the source).",
  "1 partner(s)/contact(s) are archived in Odoo: they come in INACTIVE (kept for history; nobody can pick them on new documents).",
  "1 product(s) are archived in Odoo: they come in INACTIVE (their stock and vendor prices keep a product to point at).",
  "1 product/vendor pair(s) have Odoo quantity price breaks (E-COM07/12 ×2): the lowest-quantity price is the vendor price; the breaks are in provenance.json (M_ProductPriceVendorBreak is not in this set).",
  "3 stock line(s) sum several Odoo quants of one product in one location (lots: FURN_8855 ×3, FURN_5555 ×2, FURN_8522 ×8).",
  "16 stock line(s) carry an Odoo lot (in provenance.json): the lot → attribute set instance step is not in this set yet.",
  "1 stock line(s) are NEGATIVE in Odoo (E-COM11): exported as Odoo has them; the summary screen shows them.",
  "This Odoo has 3 companies; this export is ONLY \"My Company (San Francisco)\". Each company moves into its own ERP company — export the others with: node export.js --db odoo_messy --login admin --cutover 2026-11-09 --company 2   (My Company (Chicago)) | node export.js --db odoo_messy --login admin --cutover 2026-11-09 --company 3   (Second Co Sdn Bhd)"
